\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When this passing world is done,
\par When has sunk yon glaring sun,
\par When we stand with Christ in glory,
\par Looking o'er life's finished story,
\par Then, Lord, shall I fully know,
\par Not till then, how much I owe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When I stand before the throne,
\par Dressed in beauty not my own,
\par When I see Thee as Thou art,
\par Love Thee with unsinning heart,
\par Then, Lord, shall I fully know,
\par Not till then, how much I owe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When the praise of heaven I hear,
\par Loud as thunders to the ear,
\par Loud as many water's noise,
\par Sweet as harp's melodious voice,
\par Then, Lord, shall I fully know,
\par Not till then, how much I owe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Chosen not for good in me,
\par Wakened up from wrath to flee,
\par Hidden in the Saviour's side,
\par By the Spirit sanctified,
\par Teach me, Lord, on earth to show,
\par By my love, how much I owe.
\par                              Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

